{{!
    @template mod_agora/course_card

    Card of another course of the learner: the card target's frame as a cover
    with a "stack", its state badge, and a "Broadcasts: N" overlay, the course
    name and the "Up next" substring ("On air" for a live target). The link
    leads to the same target.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * card object — data for the mod_agora/preview_card template (frame and
      badge of the target)
    * name string — course name, already passed through format_string (output
      as HTML)
    * link string — URL of the card target page
    * streams number — how many broadcasts in the course
    * next string — ready-made substring "Up next: name" or "On air: name"

    Example context (json):
    {
        "card": {
            "haslink": false,
            "cardclass": "mod-agora-preview-card mod-agora-preview-side",
            "decorative": false,
            "hasimage": false,
            "locked": false,
            "hasbadge": false,
            "srbadge": false
        },
        "name": "Financial reporting",
        "link": "https://moodle.example.com/mod/agora/view.php?id=42",
        "streams": 4,
        "next": "Up next: Cash flow statement"
    }
}}
<li class="mod-agora-card">
    <a href="{{link}}" class="mod-agora-card-link">
        <span class="mod-agora-card-cover">
            {{#card}}{{> mod_agora/preview_card }}{{/card}}
            <span class="mod-agora-card-count">{{#str}}streamscount, mod_agora, {{streams}}{{/str}}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="mod-agora-card-text">
            <span class="mod-agora-card-name mod-agora-clamp-2">{{{name}}}</span>
            <span class="mod-agora-card-sub text-muted mod-agora-clamp-1">{{next}}</span>
        </span>
    </a>
</li>
